course: dictionary
lesson: 7005
title: Helpers Who Come Fast
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A paramedic is a person, so look at the words around it to learn what they do. «Paramedics are the trained helpers who come in an ambulance.» Trained means they have learned how to help, and an ambulance is the vehicle that brings them.
explain: «Ambulances carry paramedics, who are trained to give emergency treatment on the spot and on the way to hospital.» Treatment means the help given to a sick or hurt person. On the spot means right where the person is, and on the way means inside the ambulance. So a paramedic helps first, then takes the patient to hospital.
explain: «Police officers, firefighters and paramedics are there to help children who are in trouble.» The clues help and trouble show that paramedics are helpers too. Swap in your meaning, "trained helpers who give emergency help", and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A paramedic is a trained person who gives emergency medical help.
fact: Paramedics take sick or hurt people to hospital in an ambulance.
fact: Paramedics work fast at the scene, which means the place where the accident or emergency happened.
fact: In an emergency you can call for help by dialling a number such as 999, 911, 000 or 111.
fact: Police officers, firefighters and paramedics are helpers you can count on when you are in trouble.
exercise: «Paramedics are the trained helpers who come in an ambulance.» What does paramedic mean? | *A trained person who gives emergency help | A person who sells ambulances | A doctor who works in an office | A driver who only drives ambulances
exercise: «Paramedics treated him at the scene.» What does at the scene mean? | *At the place where the emergency happened | After the patient had gone home | At the hospital, in a bed | Far away, on the other side of town
exercise: «Ambulances carry paramedics, who are trained to give emergency treatment on the spot and on the way to hospital.» What do paramedics do on the way to hospital? | Take photos of the accident | Drive the ambulance only | *Give emergency treatment to the patient | Sleep and rest
test: What does «call the paramedics» mean? | Tell a teacher about a school trip | *Ask for trained emergency helpers to come | Phone a friend for a chat | Buy a new ambulance for the school
test: Which number might you dial in the UK to call an ambulance in an emergency? | 500 | 404 | *999 | 123
exam: What is a paramedic? | A teacher who helps children with reading | A police officer who stops traffic | Someone who only sells medicine in a shop | *A trained helper who gives emergency medical help and takes people to hospital
